#passage(("If it is true that they lied about the shape of the earth, which I don't see the reason anyways, but let's say hypothetically they did, how did you make that connection that therefore now God is true? One issue, which is them lying about the shape, and the issue of it being the center, are two separate things. Let's say they lied about the shape of the Earth and they lied about it being the center: still, how is that positive evidence for the existence of God? It is not that it proves that God exists, because there is no correlation, and it's not that it proves the Christian God, because there's also no correlation. But it proves that there is a verse, or two verses, or three verses that are accurate in the Christian Bible; that's all that it really proves. You cannot make this jump into that it proves God.", "The reason those Christians are Flat Earthers is because they believe in the Bible, not because it really is flat. They believe in the Bible, and they want to view things from that perspective. They don't need to lie to you from that perspective, because tons of verses in the Bible already are scientifically inaccurate. Why do they need to go specifically into the shape of the Earth? They've already proved the Bible inaccurate through innumerable mistakes that it has that contradicts science. If you go to Job Chapter:10, Verse:10, for example, it talks about the Human Being being curdled like cheese, and milk. They can just use these verses. Why do they need to disprove the Bible, which is already disproved from that factual perspective, if you want to compare it with science? But the fact is that the cultish people that are Christians WANT to prove that verse in the Bible, while the overwhelming majority of Christians will say: \"Oh, these are metaphorical. You're not understanding them the right way.\" But either way, it does not prove God or the Christian God, whether it was the case that they lied or not.", "I'm not talking about Christianity, I'm talking about the group of conservatives. Extreme conservatives, to be clear. The overwhelming majority of Christians don't believe the Earth is flat, actually. They all believe this is metaphorical, just like they say everything else is metaphorical: Adam and Eve, and Evolution. They just accept what Science says. The reason that most Christians are rejecting it, it's because most people, in general, accept the pictures of planet Earth and what they're taught in school. An overwhelming majority of people accept what they've been taught. That's why the overwhelming majority of Christians would believe it is round.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Tyson Hockley Grills The Muslim Lantern With Difficult Questions! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XGBP8LOEhg8", ((2310, "38:30–40:07"), (2413, "40:13–41:15"), (2491, "41:31–42:57"),), id: 5041)

