#passage(("According to Islam the world was created: Allahﷻ said \"Be\" and it is (YaSin36:82). Allahﷻ, God says \"Be\" and it is, and it's very similar to the beginning of Genesis (1:3), \"Let there be light\". We believe Allah created it on a period of six days; it's very similar in the Old Testament. In this period, Allah created the Universe; in it, created what we call the Heaven, which is above us, and he made seven layers of it. Then he created Paradise, he created Hellfire, He created planet Earth, He created Angels; all of these things are things that God created. That is what it means to be All-Powerful: that you can say \"Be\" and it is! That is what it means to be All-Knowledgeable: that you can create these complex systems just by willing their existence. This is what God is.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Christian Attempts To Explain The Concept Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y0EuiG8SUZM", ((540, "9:00–10:08"),), id: 5042)
