#passage(("Once the universe is created, then, let's say 50 million years ago, God can place dinosaurs on it. Hypothetically, by the way; I don't accept or reject the existence of dinosaurs. But I'm just pointing out that it doesn't contradict what I said in any way. After the creation of the universe, we don't know when that is concluded. So we don't know the age of the earth exactly. It doesn't matter what science says. This is speculation, because it's not based on the scientific method, because you have to go back in history. It's not things which you can put under a microscope and know for sure the exact dating. That's why it changed. So we don't know exactly how old the Earth is, but my point anyway is: the existence of dinosaurs or nonexistence does not contradict Islam in any way.", "Allah doesn't tell us specifically when. There's some scholars that hold the position that there was even creation before the humans, before Adam was sent to earth; there were other creation even on Earth. Anyways, whether there was or there wasn't, there wasn't a specific time where we're told: it was this year. That doesn't really change anything. It doesn't influence anyone's life or change theology in any way. So it's not useful information for God to tell us, so we're not told about it.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim Rationally Gets Atheist To Switch His Position! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eEdpSzTw1Ks", ((833, "13:53–14:33"), (885, "14:45–15:22"),), id: 5043)

