#passage(("When it comes to Evolution, it's not a black and white thing, and the problem is: a lot of people have not studied it; that's why they don't understand why it's not a black and white thing. When you say Evolution, first there's a difference between \"Evolution\" and \"Darwinian Evolution\", because there are different types of Evolution. There are different theories of Evolution, and some of these are adopted by some people in the scientific field today in the West among atheists, and some others are adopted by others, so they don't all agree on one Theory or one understanding of Evolution. Then you have, for example: is it one origin? Is it multiple origins? The idea of Gradualism; all of these things, they disagree among one another, to begin with. But when people say \"Evolution\", just the word \"Evolution\", that things can evolve, or that things can adapt to their environments, is not a problematic concept from an Islamic perspective.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “American Questions Muslim On Free Will In Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6uEKa9ZO9u4", ((476, "7:56–8:37"),), id: 5046)
