#passage(("This seems like university students asking this individual: do Muslims believe about evolution? What Muslims were celebrating for Darwin's theory? Which scholars were talking about Darwin's theory? This is the issue where you have a lot of people, unfortunately: instead of submitting their will to Allahﷻ, they're submitting into the Western man. They're submitting into, quote-unquote, what they would call \"western science\", and what the western science says: those people are scientists, they know what they're talking about. And they always have this game they play with Evolution, they say \"all scientists agree\". No, not all scientists agree. There's a whole website about a [Third Way] of scientists that disagree, are skeptical. 1000 scientists, I believe, that wrote, and there is a specific website about it as well, that wrote their dissent towards Evolution and how they're skeptical about it. Then you have all of the other scientists which they will call them Creationists, and they will kick them out from their job, because they're opposing Evolution and they believe that human beings were created, they did not evolve. And then they will try to tell you \"all scientists agree that evolution is true\". No, that's not it. You just shame anyone else who disagrees with you, and you just highlight and give Oscars to the one who agree with you.", "And then you get these Muslims, sadly, who try to pretend as if Islam was always with Evolution. No, the Quran doesn't talk about Evolution, and it's explicitly against the idea that Adam or the human beings evolved. There is no such thing as him evolving and human beings evolving from animals. If you believe that, that's a different story; that's not what the Quran says. And there is no such thing in the Hadith; there's no stories about Evolution in the Quran. So to try to pretend that all Muslims were celebrating, that's completely disingenuous. What muslim scholars have been mocked by Christian scholars for believing in evolution?", "He's now going to show us Quran being very specific about Evolution, according to him. All the Quran talking about is stages that human beings went through (Almuminun23:14): that the human beings were sperm, and then they developed into a مضغة (Mudgha: like a chewed substance), then علقة ('alaqa: something that is like a leech), and all of these things. And then the human being is formed, and then the bones, and then the flesh on the bones. This is what the Quran is talking about, which is all about embryology, where Allahﷻ is speaking about: (Assajdah32:7) وَبَدَأَ خَلْقَ الْإِنسَانِ مِن طِينٍ (He started the creation of humans from a substance like clay), which is the creation of Adam, which has nothing to do with Evolution or anything close to it. Then it says (Assajdah32:8) ثُمَّ جَعَلَ نَسْلَهُ مِن سُلَالَةٍ مِّن مَّاءٍ مَّهِينٍ (Then Allahﷻ created his progeny from a liquid), a liquid which is referring to the sperm, or the semen. So this is what the Quran is talking about; what are you talking about, stages of Evolution in the Quran?", "The Quran is talking about the living things are made of water, in Chapter:21 (Alanbiya), Verse:30, وَجَعَلْنَا مِنَ ٱلْمَآءِ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ حَىٍّ. How is that related to Evolution? Which Evolution is saying that? I don't know this individual, but this is clearly a bunch of nonsense, and it's sad to see. And I hope Muslims don't just bend down to what people in the West believe: oh, they believe it, they accept it, therefore now we have to submit to them. We have our own positions, we know Islam is The Truth, we have evidences why the Quran is true. Anything which would directly oppose the Quran, we completely reject it, as simple as that. You have to be firm and strong upon your stances as a Muslim. He's saying the Quran says everything has gone under Evolution except God. There's no such thing in the Quran. How could you just make things up as you go like this?",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Clip-React| Bible Hasn't Changed? Quranic Evolution? Can't Trust The Prophet? | Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-UhfvmM2IY8", ((796, "13:16–14:48"), (891, "14:51–15:38"), (948, "15:48–17:12"), (1047, "17:27–18:33"),), id: 5047)
