#passage(("This is like a huge stretch! It's not about what you offer me. I'm not interested in what you're offering me, or whoever is offering me, because I'm not the one who sets the rules here. It's not like: \"I'm going to give you some ideas, and then you think about the ideas, and then let's change Islam now into this idea.\" It doesn't work like that in Islam. Islam is a strict system. When you propose something, it's irrelevant, because the rules of Islam are already set in stone. This is how Islam works. Islam is not where someone is going to come and present his own ideology, and then we're going to twist and change things based on what that individual thinks. There have been many people in history trying to do this. This is not something new. Islam has set rules, and not only Islam, language has set rules: people take the apparent literal meaning unless there's evidence that leads you otherwise.", "Now, the first thing is the soup, the \"scientific soup\" that they believe in, that brought the beginning of life, has nothing to do with Adam. It's referring to a fish in the beginning. You have a first cell that then, later on, becomes a fish, and then that fish starts walking in the land, and then that fish on the land becomes multiple things, and these things become multiple things. And then from a normal birth between two beings, you have Adam coming! You don't have a direct Creation without mother or father, which the Quran is describing. So that's the first issue that you would have. The second issue that you would have: if you were to accept that stretch that you made, it doesn't mean that Allah created you with the Hand. When He says \"with My Hand\" there, He's referring to a very specific thing that He's saying to Satan: Why are you not prostrating to that which I created with my Hand? (Saad38:75). If Allah creates everything with His Hand, then Satan would say: \"But You created me with Your Hands as well! You created everything!\" So Allah is speaking here about something that was special, that Adam was given, that other beings were not given, that Direct Creation that was given by God. Now the stretch is not going to work for that second reason.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Claims The Qur'an Contradicts Science?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7tq4SvKcBbs", ((516, "8:36–9:31"), (579, "9:39–10:44"),), id: 5050)
