#passage(("We don't look at possibilities unless there's evidence to look at them. Unless Evolution is true, we do not then see whether the idea of the existence of God could be influenced by that thing. If there is no evidence it's true to begin with, then we do not include it as a possibility to begin with.", "You can try this: socialisation and brainwashing. Go to university, or your basic friends, the people around you that are in their 20s, and just ask them, \"Is Evolution a fact?\", and all of them will say yes! And ask them the basic questions about Evolution, and they will all probably give the same answers. They've been socialised into believing in something that they do not understand. To believe in something and to be convicted with it, you need to understand at least its basics and the reasoning why you believe. If you're convicted of something, as people in the West are convicted of Evolution, and they don't know why they are, this is what brainwashing is! Because if I start asking someone for the basics of that thing that they're convicted of, believing in so much, they don't know it. If you go to a Muslim who is so convicted in Islam and says that it's the absolute Truth, and then you ask him what the 5 pillars of Islam are and he doesn't know, or these basic knowledge things, like \"What books do you guys read?\", and he doesn't know the Quran, then that becomes ridiculous. Because how are you convicted in that thing, unless you're being brainwashed to believe in that thing? You literally do not know the basics.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Attempts To Challenge Muslim Then It Backfires! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=hA_fqvgV8sU", ((1134, "18:54–19:06"), (1155, "19:15–20:31"),), id: 5056)
// U ML148:62-179 | The Muslim Lantern | 5
#passage(("To completely close this argument: science is something that is changing, that is based on the scientific method, which is to look at natural things, physical natural things that are made from atoms or matter: you observe them, the things that you can put under a microscope. So you do experimentation, repeatability and falsification. That is a scientific method. So it's the study of the natural world through experimentation, repeatability and falsification. That's the definition of the scientific method, which, by the way, was developed by a Muslim. He's called Hassan ibn alHaytham. He's the one who modernised it and developed the way we're using it today, in his book: Optics. We have no issues with the scientific method, but to talk about things which happened thousands of years ago, that's not science, that's philosophy.", "So what a lot of people don't know is that the theory of evolution is not based on real science; it's based on assumptions and philosophy, where they keep telling you: \"oh, they were doing this\", \"they moved from this river to that river, and they were eating this, and they were behaving that way\". There is no physical, natural evidence for any of that. These are all assumptions. And that's why it keeps changing. So they have a narrative, and they keep changing the narrative when they find new evidence. They will reinterpret the evidence to fit the narrative of what they already believe in. That's why you have Darwinism, Neo-Darwinism. Every other day, there is a new name for the theory of evolution. And the reason, it's simple, is because they rediscover things that are opposite to the theory. And sooner or later, you'll have a big group of scientists that will just leave that, and they will come up with a new branch: third way evolution, genetic evolution, this evolution, that evolution. They will just keep doing that, because it's not standing. So I completely reject it as a bunch of mostly nonsense. Of course, there are things which are accurate. Nobody comes to you with just nonsense. You have to mix truth with falsehood. But it's certainly not what they are portraying it to be.", "Evolution is not falsifiable, by the way. That's why it's not science. Whichever evidence comes against the current theory, they change the theory to fit that narrative, which would mean it's not falsifiable. I'll give a basic example. First, they believed in gradualism, that the evolution has to happen in a gradual process. Darwin believed in that in his book, Origin of Species. In chapter six, he mentions the possible problems that can come up with his theory, and he says that gradualism is necessary. And he talks in his books as well about the problems that he finds with the fact that there are these fossils that are very advanced in their evolutionary state, but they're very old. And it's supposed to be: the deeper you go in the earth, the less advanced this creature will be. And there's many, many examples: they show ants, and they show other fossils of these things. They're very, very, very old, but they are very, very advanced. So there's something called the Cambrian explosion.", "They have a problem: Gradualism is having an issue. The evidence is showing that gradualism is not necessarily true. So what do we do now? We say that \"oh, there is like a pattern, or there is this or that: some beings, they evolve quickly, and some beings don't evolve.\" So what they do is they re-change the whole dynamic of that essential thing that was in the theory, to fit the new evidence. So that is not science. Why? Because you cannot falsify that. The more evidences that come that are against your theory, the more you will change your theory to fit the evidence. And the reason you do that is because you already believe in the theory. How science is done is you discover evidence, and then you build a conclusion based on the evidence. You don't already have a conclusion and you change the conclusion when you find evidence against what you believe. It's not falsifiable, and therefore it's not science to begin with. It's just people who believe in something and they try their best to find an excuse for it.", "Anyone who wants a demonstration of that, just look at science: go from the start of the theory and just look down the years. They will tell you this is science. No, that's not science. Yes, science is changing, but it changes based on the evidence. On the other hand, you don't change based on the evidence. You try to fit the evidence into a narrative you already accept and believe is true, which is that evolution is a fact. People don't study these things on a scientific point, proper scientific, even on a surface level. I'm not a scientist, but I know enough to know that this is a bunch of nonsense. A lot of people are sheep. They just follow whatever people tell them to go.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Challenges The Muslim Stance On Evolution! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=daoNeH70SF0", ((201, "3:21–4:05"), (249, "4:09–5:35"), (355, "5:55–6:57"), (422, "7:02–8:01"), (486, "8:06–8:58"),), id: 5057)
// U ML360:1230-1332 | The Muslim Lantern | 7
#passage(("It's a very important thing that we need to keep in mind: the rational problems with this idea of Evolution. Number 2: it is not falsifiable. The theory of Evolution is not science; actually, it's linked to the first point that I want to make, that it's PSEUDOSCIENCE. They change the goalpost, they come up with a new name, a made-up name, to try to explain whatever happened, which means that there is nothing in that theory that is falsifiable to begin with, and this is a huge rational problem that makes it not science to begin with! Why? Because they rely on the presuppositions of Naturalism! Everything has to be explained through natural processes; they don't accept that there could be anything unnatural, metaphysical, that explains the phenomena that happens, based on that false assumption that they already started with. I already showed you that with the Cichlid Fish; I've already showed you that with the Fossil Record, how, when the Cambrian explosion happened, they change it; how, when we show them that Homology is not due to Common Ancestors, they change it; how we show them it's not due to environment, they change it, they change the name. Every evidence that they would put forward, they will change, and they will claim as if the theory is still valid.", "Evolution and its crux and its understanding is not a scientific theory. Why? Because it's PSEUDOSCIENCE: it is not something that you can see, you can observe. I cannot observe species changing from one to another; they claim because of Gradualism. We already refuted this idea of Gradualism, but they will still use it as evidence: \"oh yeah, because of Gradualism you cannot see\"! OK, you claim that there are some species who can evolve quickly: why are no species today evolving quickly, so we can observe them and see the changes that take place? So it is pseudoscience, because it's not under the scientific method, it's not under experimentation, repeatability and falsification. I cannot experiment under species that's changing from one to another, I cannot repeat the experience, and I cannot falsify the theory, because whatever you come up with, you will claim it is something else.", "All of this idea of Homo Habilis, Homo Erectus, all of that: they have chapters of stories, \"oh, the Homo Habilis who was walking in this part of the region, he met the Homo...\" All of these fictional stories they have, it's pseudoscience, it's not science; that's not how science is conducted. You don't find a tooth, and then say that there was this creature that existed, and he was walking, he was mating, and he was in this region, based on finding a tooth! That's not science! You can call it philosophy, call it whatever you want, but the theory of Evolution is not a scientific theory to begin with.", "The reason behind the demonstration that we put forward is to make this idea clear in the minds: if something is unfalsifiable, you cannot ask me to falsify it to begin with! That's why you have to ask them for the evidences for them claiming it is true to begin with. Because all of the evidences are refuted, and they're all manipulated. So if I have a building that is falling apart, you cannot focus on which part of the rocks that are problematic; the whole building is falling apart, and if there is no evidences for it, it's not science to begin with. That's why whenever you go to one thing, they will move on to a different thing, to a third, a forth thing.", "Now another thing is the idea of Randomness. We've already refuted there is no Blind Natural Selection or Random Mutation, but the idea of Randomness itself: Randomness doesn't exist in reality. You cannot prove to me that Randomness exists. Randomness is basically the lack of our explanation. If I flip a coin, it's not 50/50%; I just do not know how much pressure I'm putting in, I do not know the gravity, I do not know which side I'm pushing the coin. If I were to know all of these factors, then there is no such thing as Randomness. The whole theory is based on Randomness, and if the idea of Randomness itself is wrong, you cannot base your theory on something which doesn't make any sense, because nothing is random. Everything is happening in a causal chain, according to your beliefs, if you're a Naturalist. So you cannot pick and choose and claim: I'm a Naturalist when it comes to this part, but when it comes to this part, I'm not going to accept Naturalism, I'm going to claim that there is this hidden force is called Chance and Randomness.", "The whole theory is built on assumptions, as we said. The Tree Of Life is based on the Genes and Homology, and we showed that the Genes and Homology are not evidences for anything: Homology is not evidences for Common Ancestry, and the Genes are not similar as they claim that they are. So where this whole idea of Tree Of Life comes from? It all falls apart! Abiogenesis: it is an assumption they cannot explain. Where is the start of all of that? How did Carbon start to grow hands and legs? And hands and legs started working, and we've got what we have today!", "The idea of the changes in science: they would claim that all of these changes, all of these articles that you provided, is evidences for us, because it shows how science's changed! This is the biggest nonsense that they will come up with. Never accept this garbage from them. This is true IF you have already pillars, foundations of the theory are indisputable, and then you've got branches that sometimes happen, that need explanation, that you might explain in an evidential way; that's what a science is. Do not make them come and break the whole thing: \"And because science is changing, we're going to change the nonsense every day, a bit by bit, and this is science!\" Do not be fooled by that, Muslims, because this is a very common nonsense that they will come up with. They will come and say this is science, and science is changing. No, it's not that! It is that you've got no evidence to begin with, you've got no foundation of the theory, you've got nothing that is well established so we can base on it the theory. So never accept this nonsense of what they would call \"changes of science\".",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslims Scientifically And Rationally Dismantle Evolution! Muhammed Ali & @SubboorAhmadAbbasi”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3TrwJOx-kUM", ((4609, "1:16:49–1:18:34"), (4737, "1:18:57–1:19:40"), (4785, "1:19:45–1:20:10"), (4827, "1:20:27–1:20:54"), (4859, "1:20:59–1:21:49"), (4915, "1:21:55–1:22:28"), (4969, "1:22:49–1:23:49"),), id: 5058)
