#passage(("Evolution doesn't explain anything, because I could ask you one question, just one question: where did the first cell come from? Even they don't think it makes sense, by the way. So you have this person: he and Richard Dawkins repeated this, and he quoted him; I'm just missing his name right now, Francis Crick. So don't quote me on that exactly. But you'll find Richard Dawkins' video where he says Aliens could have put the first cell on Earth! So they're willing to accept that it could have been an Alien, because it's impossible, essentially, if you look at how unstable amino acids are. And then you have left-handed and right-handed, and you need one type to make one protein. And then you have millions of proteins in the smallest cell. Then you have the cell surviving or they're multiplying. And then you have the environment. Essentially it cannot happen. So they know that it cannot happen, and therefore, even those Atheists and four Horsemen or whatever, they'll say Aliens did it! So if they're saying Aliens could have done it, I got nothing to say at this point! This theory called \"Panspermia\": the Aliens dropping the first cell out there is called Panspermia.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Is God Necessary? Intellectual Atheist Challenges The Muslim Understanding Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bOPzUt3vmGs", ((1954, "32:34–33:56"),), id: 5059)

=== 88.5 The fossil record, gradualism and the Cambrian explosion
