#passage(("We've got what we call \"evidence\", I'm putting it in quotation marks for a very important reason. This is what people in the Darwinian field will present to you as evidence. I don't know if there's anything else that we can consider to be evidence anyways, but let's say this is the bulk of what is considered to be evidence. These are the most important things: Fossil Record, Vestigial Organs, Homology, and the Natural Selection, the blind processes that happen based on your environment for survival and reproduction. We've got Random Mutations: the Mutations happen randomly. And then we've got Similarities In Genes, Humans and Chimpanzees and different animals with each other. Lastly, we're going to talk about some Rational Problems that we have; the Theory Of Evolution as a theory.", "Darwin, when he put his theory, in chapter:6 of his book \"Origin Of Species\", chapter:6 \"Difficulties in the theory\", he put this chapter about the problems and difficulties that can come up with his theory. And he said something interesting here. He said: \"but, as this Theory innumerable transitional forms must have existed\". He put forward this thing which every Evolutist comes up to us with as well. They say that there's thousands of creatures, thousands of animals, thousands of things which have evolved over a long gradual period of time, and gradual process that took billions and millions of years. Why is this important now? Because when we ask them, can you show us a transitional creature TODAY that has evolved? They always use this excuse of Gradualism! So when it suits them they say \"Oh this takes thousands and thousands of millions of years\". But when it doesn't suit them, they say \"Oh yeah we don't have to believe it, it's a long process!\" You will see in everything that they present there's a contradiction. They self-contradict in every action that they do.", "So Darwin here said that we need to have this massive amount of Fossils of transitional creatures. You've got the Cambrian, etc. All of these are the different levels in the soil, and because it was a gradual process, when we go in the first one, we will see the latest creatures that have evolved. When you go deeper and deeper, you'll find less evolved creatures the more you go deep. So, this is what the theory is, this is a general understanding of how the Fossil Record works.", "Darwin himself knew that we're not finding all of these transitional forms. He is making the claim, not us! He's saying that they must exist based on the idea of Gradualism and slow Evolution. Then he says \"why do we not find them embedded in countless numbers in the crust of the earth?\" He's asking a question on our behalf, we don't need to ask the question he's asking! Now, how did he answer the question? It is hilarious how he answered the question. He said, it will be more convenient to discuss this question in the chapter on the imperfection of the Fossil Record. He made a chapter; he said the Fossil Record is not perfect. How does that justify your theory or anything that you said? That has nothing to justify your theory, that cannot amount to the claim that you make that there is innumerable amount of Transitional Forms and creatures. We need to find them! When we're finding all of these creatures, we need to be finding all of these Fossils that lead us, for a fact, the Evolution took place. Why are we not finding them?!", "Then we had a very interesting thing that brought even more problems on this idea, which is the idea of the Cambrian Explosion. We've got Pre-Cambrian and then Cambrian. We found so many Fossils from that period and all of these Fossils, they do not support the idea of Gradualism and that creatures took all of this time to evolve. This Trilobite is an example that we found from the Cambrian Period. This is a very advanced creature, with multiple different eyes, and it has nothing to do with the idea that this gradually evolved. We shouldn't be finding it in the Cambrian Period! We should be finding it maybe in the Tertiary Period, or one of these different periods, but it should not be in the Cambrian Period. This is one example; we find multiple different Fossils. And what this did? It completely destroyed this idea of Gradualism! Now, no longer we can accept this idea of Gradualism. They had to find the solution: how can we find deep within the Earth, in that very very long period, this extremely evolved \"creatures\"? How can we explain these phenomena? How can we account for that?", "Then what do we find? We find someone like Stephen Jay Gould. In his book \"The Panda's Thumb\", what he says is: \"It is sudden appearance of species\"! Can you explain why? Can you explain how? So what they started saying is that: \"It's not that all of these things have evolved, because we found different things like Ants for example that have not evolved.\" All of these different Fossils from the Cambrian period, there's no explanations for them. So what they did is that they shifted the goal post, they said \"Some creatures will have sudden appearance, Sudden Evolution, quick sudden Evolution, while the other ones will take a gradual and transitional period\". What is the justification? We found something that goes against our Theory, now we're going to shift and twist and change what we were saying into trying to fit this new information into our Theory!", "But this has a lot of problems. As we said, they're not giving us why. Not giving us reasons and evidence behind them giving this idea that some of them are like this and some of them are like that! The second thing is how? How would an animal or a thing evolve very quickly, suddenly, by itself, by random processes? How does that happen? This is a big issue now, because they were giving the excuse of Natural Selection, this happens over a long period of time based on the environment. So how can you account for this very sudden perfect Evolution, if you want to use that term, that happens at a certain time suddenly?! How can you explain that? And what we would say is: it's impossible to explain!", "For example, animals like giraffes, what they said is that they didn't have that long neck, they were trying to eat from the trees, so they were extending their neck, extending, and through a gradual process their legs started stretching! How ridiculous these things happen when you start to actually listen to their claims! And then it started to stretch until they started reaching the leaves and started eating from the food! Now what is the problem there? If we assume Sudden Evolution, are you trying to say to me that the blood vessels, the bones, tissues, the heart, everything related to blood evolved suddenly all together in the perfect manner and the giraffe is not going to die?! Let alone now to go to speak about the breathing system of the giraffe and all of these things. If there's a sudden Evolution that took place, how come that all of these organs and everything in the body changes in the perfect way? In the perfect time? For that creature to survive without any external factors? I want to ask Stephen Jay Gould, if he was here: Can you account for how it is possible for an animal like a giraffe, which has all of these massive changes? If you look at the blood system for a giraffe, how the blood goes from the heart to the brain in all of this long neck, you'd be shocked! Are you telling me that, \"Oh just random, chances\"?!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslims Scientifically And Rationally Dismantle Evolution! Muhammed Ali & @SubboorAhmadAbbasi”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3TrwJOx-kUM", ((258, "4:18–5:03"), (317, "5:17–6:30"), (394, "6:34–6:59"), (426, "7:06–8:10"), (490, "8:10–9:27"), (571, "9:31–10:23"), (630, "10:30–11:13"), (676, "11:16–12:38"),), id: 5060)
