 who believes in evolution, cannot present anything to show us that there was actual evolution taking place. In fact, if I were to ask you the basic question, starting point, what you call evolution: you know what [abiogenesis] is? Can you tell us where did that cell come from? Do you know how complex a cell is? The smallest cell, bacteria cell. Where did it come from? How did we have this change from chemistry to biology, like it's magic [popping] out of existence or something? How did that happen? And how did that cell survive anyway, or multiply, or then change? How did any of that happen?", "I don't need to reconcile anything, because you've presented zero evidence. In fact, what you presented me is I don't know, when I ask you about basic things, the start of the theory. But it's not you. It's the scientist. All scientists say that. They cannot answer it. So, it's not your fault. It's their fault, because they just made this up anyway. It's not a claim until you present evidences. That's what made up is: I can call something false if you're not presenting me evidences for it. If I say to you there's a pink flying elephant over there and you tell me you just made that up, that is not you making a claim. That's you refuting the claim which I already made. So that's exactly what I said when I said they made it up. So turning the table doesn't work here. It's just common sense. None of the atheists are able to provide us evidence for this. Therefore our position as Muslims, we don't need to reconcile. Why do I need to reconcile something which nobody has presented the evidence for? Now my recommendation is actually to do a bit more study and research, not necessarily on the evolution, because it's mostly a waste of time in my personal opinion, but rather on theology, a little bit on the existence of a creator, on [what] you're doing here on earth.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Atheist Attempts To Use A Christian Argument Against Muslim But Fails Miserably! Muhammed Ali