 but they don't care and they want to push forward whatever they believe in?", "There are other ideas that we have of the Human tail, that say Humans are born with tails, and these [tails] used to be from Apes and from all of these different types of animals. And in the end, it is a disease called \"Lipoma\", and there are many different names for that specific disease; it's a skin disease where you have an extra part of the skin coming out. What I'm trying to show here is when they do not have evidence for something, because they worship this thing as a religion (that's why I compare them with Christianity, they worship it to be a religion, and their idea and their understanding, this is like a religion), so if I don't have evidence for something that I already believe in, then I will make up evidence to support what I believe.", "Now moving on to what we'd call Fictional Characters. Do you know when they say it is the first appearance of Homo-Sapiens? How long ago? 200,000 years! 195 and 5 give or take. So this is what they say. This is the common knowledge, this is what people are spreading. If you go to a person, this is what they will say to you. So Nature Magazine Research: earliest appearance is 195, give or take 5 years. It's in this article by Nature. We said 200. Now they found one that is 300,000 years. \"Moroccan Fossil Rearranges Homo-Sapiens Tree\". These 200 years Gap that they have, they have the whole Family Tree based on it! Now we have to understand the significances of these changes. It's not as simple as OK yeah it was 200 and going to be 300. No! The whole Theory is based on that. The whole Evolution of the Human is based on that, because they have this Gradualism and they have these periods: this person was in this specific period of time, this animal transitions from here to there, it gradually evolved in this specific way. So it's not just simple changes, this has to rearrange the whole Family Tree!", "So they said 300 000 years. So it's not