s not 200 years, it's not 300, it's not 780, it's not 3.5, it's not 6.7. And also in Asia, because some of them are saying all of these ones are found in Africa. No! There is a Chinese Bone that is found that is also older. So what we have here is fictional stories, or fictional trees, or fictional and transitional creatures in fictional times, that they put forward to the people, and they start drawing and they start rearranging for you one by one, telling you: Look! this is now the tree of the Human Family! I think the tree of Pokemons has been rearranged less than this!", "We have here fictional characters. I'm not going to even bother to read the first name; that's why they called it Lucy, they changed the name from that name to Lucy! So those are the 4 main ones that they use today. They moved away from most of the other ones, and now they focus on those 4 main ones: Homo Habilis, Homo Erectus, Homo Neanderthalensis and Lucy. So Lucy here, there is an article from Science Daily, it says, actually, it has an Ape-like brain. And the rest of the bones that they have, they actually collected from different things: collecting a bone from here, a bone from there, a bone from a different country, and then assembling them together to try to have a Human looking-like creature that evolved from something. Today you can do that: you can bring a little head of a monkey and a hand of a Human being, a [tail] of a rat, and then gather them together and say that this was a creature that was evolving! So they themselves say actually: No, that's not from Homo-Sapien Tree, it has an Ape-like brain.", "We move to the Homo Habilis, the same thing: Ape-like bones. We move on to the Homo Erectus, it's the same thing. There's a whole research showing you how the Homo Erectus is sinking, because it's from \"erect/erecting\", so they're even making fun about it, they're even mocking their own evidences! So it's sinking, there is no evidence for the Homo Erectus as people are claiming. And here in this Nature Article, it says to you it could be from Homo Sapiens actually, it could be included in Homo Sapiens' Tree. It's not really Homo Erectus, this is actually from the Tree of the Homo Sapiens. You look at another research, in Life Science.", "The point I want to do is this: I don't want to leave to anyone excuses, later on coming and saying: OK but what about this? But what about that? I'm going to give you a crazy amount of forgeries, a crazy amount of lies, a crazy amount of what they claim to be the evidence, how they themselves admit that it's not evidence for anything, and they still come to you trying to convince you that this is some sort of an accepted fact! \"Homo Erectus Facts About The 'Upright Man'\": I opened the same link a while ago. This part called \"lineage\" was in the beginning, but what they did is they took this part and they changed it. Why did they remove it from the beginning of the research? Because they don't want people to be reading this in the beginning: \"The Lineage and Evolutionary History of Homo Erectus and other Homo Sapiens is unclear, and it has been muddied further by recent [finds]. Homo Erectus was once thought to have first evolved from an earlier Human ancestor, known as the Homo Habilis, somewhere in East Africa.\" \"However there is much disagreement about whether these populations are actually Homo Erectus, confusing matters more after analysing the new skull.\" The point is that they don't want that to be in the first page, because if that is in the first page, what you see is just further confusion upon further confusion.", "I'm sure people have heard these names. This is what Atheists come up with talking to you about; they assume they existed. An Atheist who believes in Evolution, he starts mentioning these names to you as if they're facts. But this is what your Nature Magazines are saying! This is what your own research is saying. The last one, this is called \"the demise..\". It's the research here showing how it is demised; it is 151 research reviewed put in that research, showing you how that is the demise now of this idea of the existence of the Homo Neanderthalensis, etc.", "But the point is this: if you go to any University today, they are teaching you these things are facts. They're not teaching you that these things are contested, they're confusing: \"oh these are not bones of Humans, they're actually bones of Apes\"; what we used to say to you, it's not actually true. And all of these fictional drawings are movies that they make. Literally movies: there's a movie about Lucy, the Baboon skeleton. There's a whole movie about it, showing you how she used to live and what she used to do, and all of that is coming from an Ape brain and a collection of different Fossils from different animals, from different things! Now these fictional characters, why am I calling them \"fictional characters\"? Because they literally are! Imagine constructing a full character from a TOOTH that later on you found that it's a PIG TOOTH! Even children, they have less imagination than this. Even DC movies, they are more plausible than these things that they're putting forward!",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslims Scientifically And Rationally Dismantle Evolution! Muhammed Ali & @SubboorAhmadAbbasi”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3TrwJOx-kUM", ((766, "12:46–13:22"), (809, "13:29–13:55"), (902, "15:02–16:57"), (1029, "17:09–17:47"), (1071, "17:51–18:55"), (1140, "19:00–19:36"), (1197, "19:57–21:49"), (1313, "21:53–23:02"), (1390, "23:10–24:29"), (1475, "24:35–25:17"), (1531, "25:31–26:23"), (1590, "26:30–27:07"), (1645, "27:25–28:59"), (1744, "29:04–29:47"), (1794, "29:54–30:48"),), id: 5066)
