#passage(("Science is the study of the physical world through experimentation, repeatability and falsification. This is the Scientific Method. But consciousness, you cannot put it under a microscope, it's not a physical thing. So you will have to make assumptions about its nature and what it is.", "What you said right now contradicts what you said earlier, which is that you just pick specific things from different religions, and commonality is how you identify The Creator. But that's not a commonality between the different religions. Christianity doesn't say that. What you just described is a Buddhist belief. Maybe you've listened to someone who took his beliefs from Buddhism, but what you've just said is one of the schools of thought of Buddhism.", "When he says: \"the kingdom of God is within you\" (Luke17:21), I understand, but if you read the Bible, it does not say that; for example Genesis, the first part of the Bible, The Old Testament does not say that. I would say that you've interpreted Jesus' verse to mean that. I can give you a completely different interpretation other than what you've said. But if you want to say Jesus said that, then you have a clear verse or a clear quote from him saying \"That we're all one unity\", for example.", "Genesis is also coming from Jesus according to the Christians, because they believe he's God. So God said what he said in the beginning; so Jesus didn't only say what's in The New Testament, but because of the Trinity, he also said what is in The Old Testament. So if you read in the beginning of Genesis, it says: \"Bereshit bara' Elohim et hashamayim ve'et ha'aretz\" (Genesis 1:1). \"Bereshit\" means in the beginning. \"bara Elohim\": God created, in Hebrew, the Heavens and the Earth. So if he's saying God created the Heavens and the Earth, then God is separated from His creation, because God existed before creating the Heavens and the Earth, and He cannot be inside something that He created later on.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Iceland Visitors Enquire About Islam! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xigQO8G9dOo", ((1, "0:01–0:08"), (16, "0:16–1:12"), (83, "1:23–2:19"), (147, "2:27–3:01"),), id: 5094)
