#passage(("You're saying you're God, so I have a challenge for you as a God: Can you stop closing your eyes, can you stop flinching, for just 10 minutes? Can you do it as a God? Because God is, by definition, the All-Powerful entity. If you're not even able to stop yourself from flinching, don't tell me \"I'm a God\", because that just sounds ridiculous.", "We're not pure Consciousness. We are a physical entity that has Consciousness, which we call the Soul. We are two things, not one. This is the issue that I found with a lot of Hindus and Buddhists etc. They think physical means \"Bad\", and we just need to focus on metaphysical or Consciousness. You need to get the idea of Consciousness into your mind and become one in unity with Consciousness. I know what you're saying, but I'm disagreeing with you. I'm saying no, that's not the case. The case is, in absolute reality, in existence, where we're living as Human beings, there're two things: there is materialistic existence that we have as Human beings: flesh, blood, bones, objects, material around us; and there's also a Consciousness, a soul that is God-given by Allahﷻ. This is what we believe. But the problem is not that. The problem is you're claiming our Consciousness is the same as The Consciousness, which is God.", "You use the term God, but you don't really mean God. We use the term God differently. The unity of Consciousness, which you're calling God, is not what we call God. When we say we believe in God, we're referring to a specific thing: something that has attributes of All-Powerful, All-Knowing, Omniscient, Omnipotent, all of these attributes. This is what we mean by God. So if you use the term God and refer to it anything else other than that, we don't say that is God, we say you're misusing the term then.", "Because you're claiming you're God, when you commit murder, then you're saying: \"God murdered God.\" When someone steals, then you say: \"God stole from the other God.\" It just becomes ridiculous! If everything is God, then there is nothing else, and this is essentially the essence of your belief: that there is nothing else in existence, it's just God, there's no Humans. But we say that makes zero sense, because intuitively, as Human Beings, we know that we're separate entities. We exist, we have ideas, we have understandings, we engage with one another; this is what we know for a fact. For you to come and tell us \"you actually don't exist, you're not real\", we're not going to believe you. It doesn't make sense for us.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Hindu Monk Confronts Muslim On His Claims! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EKQreb32rcM", ((214, "3:34–4:02"), (258, "4:18–5:23"), (330, "5:30–5:54"), (364, "6:04–6:36"),), id: 5095)
