#passage(("This false ideology existed in Islam. Some people believed in it based on Buddhism. So they were influenced by Buddhism, and then they came up with this idea called Wahdat al-Wujud, the oneness of existence. So it's separate from oneness of God. So they said all existence is one: there's nothing exists except God. And this has been rejected, of course, by all traditional scholars in Islam, because I highlighted why it's irrational, but also because it opposes Islam. And this is a belief where someone is excommunicated from Islam if they hold, because basically you essentially made yourself divine and also stripped God from what God is. It's meaningless to say that I worship God.", "There were just people that traveled to India and certain places, and they were influenced by Hinduism and Buddhism, and that was later on, like years and years. That was never there in the beginning of Islam. We're talking about 6-700 years later: someone went there, got influenced by philosophy, people refuted him, and that was it. Talking about one or two or three people. We're not talking about like the Trinity or any of that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Agnostic Claims That Pantheism Is More Rational Than Monotheism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C3BXt0zJr3o", ((3197, "53:17–53:59"), (3255, "54:15–54:37"),), id: 5097)
