#passage(("I am looking for the Truth. That's the point for me: it's not that I pick and choose what I like. Buddhism, for example, and Christianity, Judaism, Islam, Sikhism: I didn't look into those religions to choose what fits my desires and what I like, and then I follow it. Because it's not about what I like, it's about what is truly from God. If God exists, and it is the truth, then God sends commands. So if there is a Creator, One Entity that created the world, that entity will send a teaching; that teaching cannot be all of these different religions. So if, for example, Islam is true, then nothing else is true; if Christianity is true, then nothing else is true. So the reality is that we need to try to see the reasons, the evidences for why a specific religion is true and another religion is not true.", "They are contradictory; there cannot be different views of God. For example, you can not say that god is an animal, like a cow, and in the same time that God is nothing like the creation. These are two contradictory statements; both of them can not be reconciled. There is something called pantheism, which is that everything is god, god is everything, so it includes the cow. The difference is Muslims believe Allah is separate from the world, so these are contradictory beliefs. I can not believe that god is everything and in the same time I believe that god is separate from the world.", "I would not say that God is under my shoes right now. That's not something that befits the Majesty of God, and I am not going to say that God is in the toilet. For me, God is a holy being, He is not everywhere. God is not the rapist. When he is raping, so god is raping? And the person being raped is god? Do you see the problems with this idea and concept of saying everything is god? It's not about what I want. Its about what god is.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “English Lady Questions Muslim On Women's Rights! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7z-KdU-s04w", ((51, "0:51–1:57"), (138, "2:18–3:19"), (203, "3:23–3:50"),), id: 5098)
