#passage(("What you're proposing right now is pantheism. We completely reject that, because that [defies] logic. If you say everything is the same, you have many issues. First, you cannot have morality. You cannot have right or wrong, cannot say this is wrong, because there's no someone. If I steal from you right now, I'm not really stealing, because it's my property. You're all the same; stealing from yourself. So there is no morality.", "Stealing, by definition, by everyone's definition, is to take [something] from one person's [possession] to the other [possession]. If I take something from you, and you and me are the same, it's not stealing, because I'm not taking someone else's [possession], it's my [possession]. This is a problem: you cannot have stealing.", "To me, language is objective. What do I mean by that is that words have meanings. [Dictionaries] have definitions of these words. Words have meanings; if they don't, they wouldn't make any sense for me and you to have a conversation. So when we say what is killing: is taking someone else's life. This is a definition. These are objective definitions. Stealing also has an objective definition. You'll never open a dictionary in the [world] and it would say \"to take [possession] from your own self\", because it's still your [possession]. It does not change; all you're doing is moving from one place to another. So again, killing would not make any sense, because you're not taking someone else's life, you're taking your own life, and it would be suicide. So killing someone else, under the pantheism, you be killing yourself.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Pantheist Challenges The Muslim View Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=m4s4GlDTg28", ((666, "11:06–11:37"), (713, "11:53–12:24"), (776, "12:56–13:46"),), id: 5099)

