#passage(("We can have disagreements, there's no issues, but the fundamental question should be, I think, how do we know about God? Is it based on our own minds? So is that God Jesus, Allah, Yahweh, Krishna? But Jesus is a human being; Allah is not a human being. Can you define what God means? \"God is that I am\": that's just a statement. What is the meaning of God? We don't bring our beliefs from the Bible. You're referring to the statement in the Old Testament to do with Moses, where he asked God about his identity, in Exodus. We're not Christians, so we're not bound by that.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Philosophers Challenge The Muslim Understanding Of God! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=agqDQQkQf2A", ((164, "2:44–4:06"),), id: 5102)
// U ML208:168-223 | The Muslim Lantern | 2
#passage(("What you said is there's many [roads] to God, many roads; all roads lead to Rome. I'll say to you, the problem with that is the following: these roads describe God differently, and God is an entity that exists, that cannot be multiple things that are contradictory. So if we go through the road of Christianity today, that would say to us [there's] something called Trinity: God the Father, God the son, God the Holy Spirit. And then we go through the road of Islam, that says no, God is just one. These two roads cannot lead you to Rome, because Rome is either three in one or just one. So first you got to identify what God is, and whatever God is, you cannot say someone who believes incorrect things about God is going to lead you to God.", "This is what we believe as Muslims: you need to investigate the truth and [search] for the truth and reach the truth. You cannot say that everything is the truth while these things are contradictory. For instance, it's either I'm talking to you right now or I'm not talking to you right now. Can it be that I'm talking to you and I'm not talking to you in the same time? No. So it cannot be that all of these religions that have contradictory beliefs in their core foundations are all accurate and correct.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Hindu Questions Muslim On Polytheism! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6Nbn5J51AtE", ((382, "6:22–7:04"), (471, "7:51–8:15"),), id: 5103)
// U ML408:57-87 | The Muslim Lantern | 1
#passage(("Exactly what you're saying right now is a Buddhist belief. Who do you listen to? Sam Harris? I know where you're coming from. This is not new to me. But the point is, we have our own beliefs, we have our own tradition, and we have evidence for what we say. And it is OK to listen to someone, but my advice would be to not blindly follow someone, because Sam Harris self-contradicts himself all the time. He is a walking self-contradiction.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Iceland Visitors Enquire About Islam! Muhammed Ali - Speakers Corner”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xigQO8G9dOo", ((220, "3:40–4:08"),), id: 5104)
