#passage(("You've got Feminism, for example, which is a horrible, terrible ideology, first wave, second wave, third wave, all of this nonsense. It had some reasoning behind it in the beginning, of how women were being treated. But it turned into this idea of hating man. \"If you get naked you're free\" somehow. I do not know: if I take my cloth off now I'm becoming free somehow! So this has become the ideology of Feminism: masculine women that hate the opposite gender, that believe they should become men, in a specific way. Now the exact opposite of that ideology is the Red Pill.", "I do agree that there is a lot of good things that they speak about, realistic things, correct things that they speak about. My claim is anything that is good will already be found in Islam, otherwise it would not even be good to begin with. But my problem with the Red Pill is this: it teaches you how to deal with the wrong type of women. This is what makes the whole ideology crumble for me. The Red Pill only teaches you how to deal with the bad type of women. It doesn't tell you how to deal with good women. And if you deal with the good type of women the same way you deal with the bad type of women, done! This woman is not going to stay with you. She's not already corrupted, with a baggage of trauma, being abused and used. It's designed to deal with women that are addicted to social media, to celebrities that have all these bodies; sex-workers, bartenders, that's what it teaches you to deal with, women who are in the club all the time.", "It sets you up for failure. The other self-contradiction is it teaches you to seek good women. So when it teaches you to marry good women, and then all the ideology is how to behave with the bad woman, you can never succeed. You can never work a good relationship with a good woman, because you've already lived all your life dealing with the bad type of women. But people in the Red Pill believe that there are no good women in the West. That's why it exi