#passage(("There is this video I've seen: there's this YouTuber called Sonny, I think he's been on Muslim channels before as well. He went to Spain and then he went to Morocco and he did public interviews with the people, asking them questions about The Alphabet Community and things related to gender and stuff like that, and the video is titled Woke versus Muslims on Pride Month. So he goes to Spain and he asked the people how many genders are there, and things like that, and can I be a transgender, etc. And then he does the same thing in Morocco, and then he shows the people the different kind of responses that he got. The issues I had with the video is, when I looked at the comments, mostly 99% is positive comments for Muslims. They're proud of the answers that the Muslims have given in the videos. And I think there is a huge issue that needs to be addressed in the video, couple of issues actually.", "We have this idea of Liberalism, which essentially just means \"you can do whatever you want as long as you don't harm anyone else\". So this is the core principle of Liberalism, which is the reason the West is on its downfall today. And then you've got the idea of Feminism, that women are strong and independent and they can do everything and they don't need a man and they're better than men and all of that. The video is supposed to show that Muslims are not following these principles. They're not following Liberalism, they're not following Feminism, they are following their own Islamic Tradition and Islamic Teachings. And the video becomes very popular; even though it's been one day, it's almost 100K views. So, Muslims are very happy about the responses. But the question is: were the responses that were given in the video actually representative of the Islamic Community, and what we believe, and what we should be saying as Muslims? But I want to also say that they went into a tourist place in Morocco, so they were talking to a specific type of Moroccan people. This is not all Moroccans and what they believe. But this is unfortunately a common belief that Muslims have today.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Muslim vs Woke | What Islam Actually Says - Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8tefi4j0jMY", ((13, "0:13–1:00"), (68, "1:08–2:26"),), id: 5130)
