#passage(("The reality is that this is the true face of some of these women, the true feministic face of some of these women. It's not about equality, but they want everything to be in accordance to what they like. If Islam doesn't give me everything, then Islam is made for men. So, if Islam gives some things for the man and some things for the woman: no, no, everything has to be accordance to my desires, or otherwise it's a religion made for men. So, a lot of these women are arguing for their own benefit. Has nothing to do with it being a religion to suit the desire of the men.", "I had a message from the sister that messaged me before, and she's like, \"I'm starting to doubt the Hadith. I don't know if I can follow the Hadith anymore. I've been seeing some shubuhat that people have been putting forward.\" So, a lot of these sisters, that are actually good sisters, they watch a lot of this content and they fall for it. They fall for these tricks. And instead of getting educated and asking and inquiring and becoming more learned, they're like, \"I'm going to reject Hadith.\" So, it's not: is the Hadith historically valid or not, and the method is correct? No, it's now that there are some things that are said in the Hadith that doesn't sound nice to me, so I'm going to reject it. In reality, what they criticize is actually something for the benefit of the women.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Is Islam A Religion Made For The Men?”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OzxyEO708yI", ((432, "7:12–7:43"), (464, "7:44–8:26"),), id: 5133)
