#passage(("He's comparing: he visited Dubai. You're visiting, you're not a citizen born in that country with a passport. This is not the same thing; you're making a false equivocation there. Then, on top of all of that, he keeps comparing Muslim countries to the West. If the both of them operate in the same way, then why are you keep claiming to us that America is superior ideologically, and you keep criticizing our countries for not having free speech and all of these things? The Muslim countries do not operate with the same laws that you operate with. You operate with the absolute idea of free speech: everyone should have free speech and freedom for religion and expression. These are your laws. So when we say there are people in your country, they are citizens of that country. They are following these laws. You cannot come and complain about a Muslim country that has different set of laws, because they operate on a different world view.", "So he keeps making the false [equivocation], the same thing he did with comparing Times Square to Mecca. Mecca is obviously a place only strictly for worship and for Muslims, so you can do pilgrimage and you can do practices of worship. People go to Mecca just to pray and do pilgrimage. That's the whole purpose of going there. We have Mecca, and all of it is a sacred place, you can say, is a haram. Now you can compare that to the Vatican or something like that. That's a closer comparison. You cannot compare Time Square, which is just a random place with billboards of advertisement.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Myron Gets Demolished In Sneako Debate After Ducking 1 on 1 Discussion! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2wy4D0RloNM", ((2807, "46:47–47:42"), (2862, "47:42–48:13"),), id: 5141)
