#passage(("I don't know how women are living in Afghanistan. Afghanistan is a war-torn country destroyed by the US. Everyone is living a very difficult economic situation because of it. I have not been to Afghanistan personally, and I'm not sure how they live their lives. So I cannot comment on something like that, that I'm not 100% sure of. But I'm pretty sure these women are happy living their lives, the way they want. Not every single one of them, of course; there's unhappy people everywhere. But they are happy; if you go to them, they'll say to you, this is our country, these are our laws. We like what we're doing. Even Trump, I think there's a video of him, he was saying: \"Leave Afghanistan! The women are happy, they've been covering for thousands of years. Why are you going to come to them and tell them not to cover?\" They're happy with their own culture and society! Who are you to come and tell them how to live their life? The US 'went out' of Afghanistan... KICKED OUT, where they couldn't do anything! They had to leave. They had no choice! They stayed there for tens of years. Them and the Russians or whatever, they couldn't!", "Where is this Wilson Center? I've never heard of it in my life. Are you telling me they went and surveyed all the women in Afghanistan, and they asked them, and they came to the conclusion that 80% of them want to commit suicide? With what method? Who did this study? You think Afghanistan allows some random people to come and survey their women, and ask them whether they want to live? This is the problem! You read things online, and you actually think that these are representatives of actual surveys that take place in reality. No, they're not!", "There is a hatred for Muslims, a demonization that takes place. You can look at studies that show you that Muslims, when it comes to the T word or whatever, they are put in the media five times more than the average person. There's an agenda to demonize our people, and to make them look barbaric, and to make them look in a certain way. Now, America wanted to go and take over the country; they couldn't! They even tried old methods of inserting people within the community, dividing the community, giving weapons. They tried everything. They couldn't! Now, what they do, due to them being sore losers, is that now they're trying other methods of demonizing these people. Because in the end, you cannot go and take over a nation unless you demonize it first. You need to do that. That's what they did with Iraq. That's why they claim there is Weapons of Mass Destruction, because then that can give them a justification. They need to demonize the people in order for them to give a justification to themselves, so when they go in these countries and destroy it and pretend that they are saving it. Every person I know from Afghanistan, even though I have not been to Afghanistan, every person I know with their families, none of them have any issues with their wives, none of their wives complain.", "If you want reports, bring reports from the country themselves. Why is American media, European media, UK media reporting about Afghanistan? It's not your country! Why are you day and night talking about them? Are you not seeing that there is something going on here? They are trying to make you think a specific way about Muslim people, or people who live in Afghanistan and have certain views. I don't know the situation of North Korea. But you do have people fleeing North Korea and then telling you what's happening to them. You don't have the same thing to show me here. Show me where are all of these people fleeing Afghanistan, telling you, \"Oh, look, we have been in the worst...\" That doesn't exist! North Korea is not a good example because of that.", "I'm not saying Afghanistan are saints. I haven't been there. But I'm saying there is definitely an exaggeration, number one, of what's taking place. Number two, the West has no right to talk to us about women or what we can and cannot do, because their morality is subjective and they're not our superiors to tell us, to lecture us about what morally right and morally wrong. Your countries are full with the reports of your own research institutes. They're full of abuse and bad treatment of women. Go to the UN. It has the biggest study that was done for women. It's called \"Women Abused, Everywhere, Every Day\", where it shows you that almost all women, at least 30% of them, are abused physically, being forced to watch pornographic material, whatever. We're saying the last person who comes and lectures us about treatment of women is the West! We don't take your word, because THE WEST IS THE BIGGEST ABUSER. Look at England, what happens when people lose football matches, and all the abuse they do to the women. So, in the end, it's a very simple thing: The West has no right to lecture us. Yes, people in Afghanistan are not perfect, but people in the whole world are not perfect. So, to focus on one incident or two incidents does not mean anything. There's exaggeration. There's agenda that is happening to make them look in a specific bad light.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Tran$gender Challenges Muslim On His Comments About LGTBQ Community! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XPGGQKYFYqo", ((1987, "33:07–34:35"), (2097, "34:57–35:28"), (2151, "35:51–36:53"), (2270, "37:50–38:52"), (2342, "39:02–40:38"),), id: 5147)

