#passage(("Is England though a Christian country? That's a good question to ask. Historically, it was a Christian country, but now I would say it's a secular country. It's not just that the majority of people are culturally Christian, meaning that the churches are empty. People do not live by the ten tenants of Christianity. But the governmental system and institutions as well do not operate based on religious law. So when you go to the court it's not based on religious law.", "I think it's a part of the equation, because you could have, even if the people are not really practicing, the government itself speaks out. For example, the government itself has crosses, the government itself has the pope in every initiation of their practices, the government continuously mentions that we are a Christian nation. If this is the case, even if the people are not, the people will sooner or later start practicing. If this is the case, you could call it still a Christian nation from that perspective, that the government is proudly representative of their own faith. So it's a part of the equation. So you can have both, or at least one, but in this case you have none.", "So now they teach you everything, and they don't necessarily tell you this is the truth and this is false. You have atheists actually teaching religious classes. They teach everything.", "But my perspective is: what you should teach the people is the truth. So just like when you are in medical school or wherever it is, you're not going to just teach different theories. If you know for a fact some of these medical theories are wrong, and we already discovered them wrong, and now we have the correct theory or the correct procedure, you're not going to teach the wrong procedure as well. You're going to teach only the correct procedure. So even when it comes to worldly things, since they teach only things which are correct, when it comes to the afterlife and truth they should be doing the same. So what should be taught in schools is that which is true. But that also, as I said, is going to be reflective of what the government follows to an extent. Since this country has become a secular country, then it has become the case: freedom of religion, freedom of speech or whatever, and an extension of that is that they in schools will teach you [whatever] you want to learn.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Confident Atheist Attempts To Make A Case Against Islam! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=mW_gKZXnhuw", ((59, "0:59–1:27"), (114, "1:54–2:29"), (149, "2:29–2:57"), (187, "3:07–4:09"),), id: 5148)
