// U ML128:151-342 | The Muslim Lantern | 8
#passage(("Now, I mentioned one issue, which is the bias, as a negative thing in Artificial Intelligence, but there are other issues. So, for example, you need to understand that there is data collection taking place! Whenever you speak with Artificial Intelligence or whatever, it collects your data. Sometimes if you upload pictures, it will store your pictures, etc. And nobody reads the privacy statements or whatever and usage of data, because it's massive articles, and they make it like this so nobody reads it. So you need to understand that your data is also being collected and is being used and sold. So you've got to be aware of that when you're asking questions or uploading personal information or data or whatever it is. It's very important.", "Other things, for example, is the age of deception that we're living in today. Even it happens often during my live streams, where people are suspecting that the people I'm talking to are either using ChatGPT or whatever Artificial Intelligence to get responses so they can continue the conversation. If a person doesn't have his camera on, it could be just the audio is generated by AI. And this is improving day by day. And people have been spreading all of these different audios of different scholars, saying: Look! The voice of the scholar; and then saying, I'm not the scholar, I'm just an Artificial Intelligence, to be aware of incorrect and fabricated voice notes and videos that are being widespread. So we're entering an age of deception. So we have to be very, very aware and very, very careful as Muslims. And in the future, we're entering this age in which some of the Narrations mentioned, depending on its authenticity, that (the person who's truthful, people will call him a liar) (and the person who's a liar, people will think he's truthful). And we're entering this age. And you can see how easy it's going to be for the Dajjal to deceive the people. It's already happening now. It was very easy for a little bit of editing, and people are already buying whatever they're seeing and thinking this is absolutely truth. So that deception is problematic.", "Also, the AI itself is trained on the arts of deception. I remember one time, I was on Twitter and there was a comment, and then Grok responded to it, and it was on my post, and then it referred to me as a \"controversial figure\" that is not objective, or something to that effect. Then I asked Grok, where are you bringing this information from? So it showed me some random Reddit post that is made by an atheist that is depressed after he had a conversation with me, and he hated his life, so he went and he made a post on Reddit. So it's used that as a source, to say I'm not objective or whatever, or I'm controversial, which is crazy! Then I asked Grok to correct this information based on the fact that this is just one source, and it's not reliable, and we don't know who's saying this, etc. So Grok said yes. Then I ended up asking Grok the same question, but from a different account. So I wanted to see: does it update information? So it did say to me, yes, we have updated information. You go to the other account, it gives you the same exact answer that it gave you before. So it's being trained on deception. That's why sometimes you get it to apologise, you get it to say that it's wrong, you get it to do ridiculous things, because these are programmes in the end. And depending on what they're programming them to do: if they're programming them to agree with you, they will agree with you, even if it's a lie; if they're programming them to disagree with you, they will disagree with you. So you need to understand these are just programmes. They're not authority, not things you can use and rely on their answers.", "Now, most importantly, one of the biggest issues that are coming very soon from AI is control. They're already using AI in YouTube, for example, to detect certain words that are being said are not appropriate or whatever. And because Artificial Intelligence doesn't understand context, it can flag a video, it can remove a video, it can strike your channel. And that can be a huge issue. I have a friend who has this payment system or whatever, and you had some artificial intelligence flagging one payment, and it shut down the whole payment processor! It's a huge issue, just because it incorrectly flagged one transaction. This Artificial Intelligence now is being used more often. So now it's replacing people. Now it's going to replace a lot of people in the future, especially in the electronic spaces. Now, when it does look at the future, what kind of future are we expecting? Imagine they put for each building or each house or the grocery store or the bank or any government institution, they just put this facial recognition thing that is based on AI, and they give you points as a citizen. And if you are being a good citizen, you can enter these specific locations. If you're not being a good citizen, you're not going to be able to. Each house has one of these systems that locks your house, and then you can be locked in your house. This has already been used in the cars and Tesla and whatever: can lock a person inside his car using Artificial Intelligence. So we're approaching an age when we need to be very, very careful about the advancements of these things, because they're not designed by Muslims. They're not designed by people who agree with you ideologically, which means that if this becomes something which has more and more control every day, it's only going to harm us as a community. So we need to be prepared. So these are all things that we need to look out for, harmful things, negative things, etc., that we need to be very, very, very careful about.", "Does that mean we should not be using Artificial Intelligence? No! I'm not saying that. There's many good usages that we can use Artificial Intelligence in. For example, translation; for example, writing articles; for example, correcting grammatical mistakes in articles; for example, data entry, coding. All of these things are OK. As a Muslim, you can benefit from Artificial Intelligence. You can use it in titles of videos or whatever. You can use all of these things, creating thumbnails. All of these are great usages of AI. So we're not anti-AI, and we shouldn't be anti-AI. We should be using it and benefiting from it. At the same time, understand where it can be used and where it cannot be used. It's a tool, just like anything else and everything else. Just think of AI like you're using Google. You're not going to trust a random site that pops up, and you don't even know who wrote that website. Just think of AI the same, because it relies on all of these different websites to collect information. So always keep that in mind, that it is not a reliable thing for you to go ask medical advice from, or for you to go ask religious advice from. [They] are very specialised fields. These things, for now, need to focus on going and asking the people of knowledge and people of understanding, and not basing it on such AI models.", "So what should we do as Muslims? The first thing we should be doing is this timeless rule in the Quran, this timeless rule which is miraculous, which shows you that the Quran is for every time, and for every people and for every culture. That the Quran tells you (alHujurat49:6): if an unknown person, if an ignorant person, if a disobedient person comes to you with the news, you need to verify it, you need to search, you need to investigate. That's what the Quran teaches you to do. Now, this rule, we need to thoroughly apply as Muslims. Because, like I said, today the deception is happening and increasing day in and day out; you need to be very aware. You cannot just trust whatever you see online. You need to research, verify, and investigate, and make sure that whatever you're seeing, whatever you're hearing, is accurate, and it is coming from the source. Because, like I said, very soon, they all talk about this island and list; it ends with \"stein\". That list, for example, if it comes out, people can just come and say later on: oh, this is AI! All of these videos are AI! So deception is going to increase very, very, very highly. So we need to be very, very thorough in our investigation and research when we see information online or things being said.", "Secondly, what else do we need to do? We need to advance ourselves in the knowledge of what these technologies are, its capacity, and developing OUR OWN. Our issue with social media is that we're reliant on non-Muslim social media, and then we're restricted, and we're having all of these issues. If we did our own social media, we didn't have this issue. So now with AI, we need to do that. We need to have our own people that are designing AI that we're using as Muslims in a way that benefits us. Because we can input our data, just like these people are inputting their data. They believe their morality is superior, and that's why their AI is going to reflect that. We can programme our own AI as well. And we need to advance ourselves in preventative measures, ways that we can protect ourselves. So perhaps advancing these AIs so we can detect videos which are AI from videos which are not AI. Probably it is going to be very difficult, but that's something that we need to work on, and try to do our best to advance ourselves in these types of fields, so we can protect ourselves as Muslims and use that as a shield. Because, like I said, once these things are being used by these governments that disagree with your morality, that want to control you, then what else can you do? You're going to be trapped. If you don't have something to protect yourself, if you're not advanced, if you're not familiar and knowledgeable about these type of systems, times are going to be very, very difficult. And we can see this advancement is probably leading us to some sort of a death of technology completely, and we're coming back to the old days. That's what it seems like it's going, because AI is replacing humans in, as I said, all of these fields. So nobody knows how the future is going to be, and what kind of influence that is going to be on human beings generally.", "And keep in mind, do not be a lazy person. Remember Prophet Muhammad, peace be upon him, he said that: \"Ignorance will widespread\", even though the Prophet, peace be upon him, said that: \"Writing will widespread\". And you can see that now with AI. People are so lazy, they don't read, they don't investigate, they don't research. You ask a guy, did you do research? He says: yes, yes. And he just went and asked AI in two minutes, and he thinks that's research. That's not research! Research is that you do it on your own. You understand what is the primary source of materials, you ask the people of expertise, etc., and you make sure that you're collecting the right information. Now people are becoming lazy and lazy every day. And you as a Muslim cannot be like that. You need to be aware, and understand that these things are limited. They have their own good usages. They have their negative and harmful aspects. And you need to be in the middle as Muslims: use it as a tool in the things in which it can benefit you, and then become more knowledgeable, advance yourself, and protect yourself from any harms possible.",), "The Muslim Lantern, “Can Muslims Really Trust Artificial Intelligence?! Muhammed Ali”", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7opfbjHoB1E", ((498, "8:18–8:54"), (536, "8:56–10:13"), (614, "10:14–11:38"), (702, "11:42–13:44"), (827, "13:47–14:54"), (898, "14:58–16:13"), (976, "16:16–17:55"), (1079, "17:59–18:51"),), id: 5179)
